  "worked_solution": "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that the global maxima of $f(x)$ are at $x=-1,3,9.$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $-1,3$ and $9.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14180691/assets/6e5f9b96a81ee467251cbe7f1792b3bb8c58bb454e2ec3684173ca798ca0f9d9.png)",
